  "body": "`crates/post/tests/` has 106 flat integration test binaries (3.46 GB for one target set, 15.7 s warm build). `crates/sim/tests/` has 87 flat integration test binaries (2.16 GB, 11.1 s warm build). Neither crate has `ISOLATED` (`xtask/src/lanes.rs`) or `SLOW_BINARIES` (`xtask/src/plan.rs`) entries.\n\nFold both crates as the pilot wave after the `xtask` directory-suite prerequisite lands:\n- Group `crates/post/tests/` into ~8–10 domain directory suites (`tests/<domain>/main.rs` with `mod <file>;`).\n- Group `crates/sim/tests/` into ~8–10 domain directory suites.\n- Keep each submodule's `Gate map` header intact so `quick` maps source modules to the matching submodule.\n\nExpected saving: ~5.2 GB disk per worktree (-92%) and ~18 s warm build on Linux (~50 s on Windows).\n\nEvidence and measurements: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/919#issuecomment-7065686766\n\nDone means: `crates/post/tests/` has at most 12 binaries, `crates/sim/tests/` has at most 12 binaries, the `#[test]` count of each crate is unchanged, and `cargo xtask gate batch` plus `xtask` asset and gate-map tests pass.\n\nPart of #919\n",
